Thanks, good catch. I agree this should be coordinated with the existing proposals rather than adding yet another overlapping knob.

I'm happy to align this PR with the direction maintainers prefer:

- if `--no-restart` from #30824 is preferred, I can rework/close this PR and use that path instead;
- if the env-var approach is preferred, I can rename this to match the existing `HERMES_SKIP_GATEWAY_RESTART` proposal from #6703 instead of introducing `HERMES_UPDATE_SKIP_GATEWAY_RESTART`;
- or I can adapt this PR into tests/docs around the chosen implementation.

The goal here is just to make gateway-hosted cron update jobs safe, not to push a specific knob name.
